    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/management-accountant-townsville-qld-australia-f49e0000-11cc-40bf-a912-4b3a3aaff1b9": {
      "title": "We're Hiring!",
      "description": "Management Accountant - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Management Accountant 495653 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Sep 6 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description James Cook University (JCU) is creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally. Are you an ambitious and skilled accounting professional looking for your next exciting opportunity where you can make a real impact? Look no further, take the next step in your career journey with our world-leading University! James Cook University (JCU) are seeking a talented and motivated individual to join our dynamic team as a Management Accountant. Full-time: 36.25 hours per week Based at the Townsville Bebegu Yumba campus Successful candidate must be based in Townsville or willing to relocate before commencement. HEWL 8: $111,960 - $128,567 per annum plus up to 17% superannuation. ABOUT THE ROLE In this role, you will support effective decision-making and contribute to the University’s financial sustainability by delivering high-quality financial management advice and services. As a key member of the financial management team, you will support budgeting and forecasting processes, develop realistic financial projections aligned with strategic priorities, and help manage finance-related risks through financial modelling, business cases and capital planning. You will also contribute to continuous improvement by developing practical financial management tools, strengthening policies and procedures, and supporting the use of business intelligence and data warehousing systems. Your analysis and insights will help maintain key financial performance metrics, interpret results for stakeholders, and ensure data integrity through accurate reporting on financial performance against targets. WHAT YOU WILL BRING TO THE ROLE You will bring relevant qualifications in business, accounting or a related field, together with a CA/CPA accreditation and contemporary knowledge of accounting standards. Your background in auditing, business consulting, financial evaluation and modelling will support your ability to provide sound, practical and value-adding advice. You will be confident in anticipating management information needs, identifying key issues, evaluating outcomes and translating financial insights into clear recommendations. Strong organisational, problem-solving and administrative skills will enable you to manage competing priorities, meet deadlines and exercise sound judgement and initiative. As an effective communicator, you will build and maintain productive working relationships, consulting and liaising confidently with staff across the University and with external stakeholders. WHY JCU? JCU offers a dynamic and culturally diverse workplace where your ideas are valued, your professional growth is supported, and your work-life balance is respected. Working under the values of Authenticity, Excellence, Integrity, and Respect , we support and empower our people through the provisions of; A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper 5 weeks of annual recreation leave plus leave loading 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year Up to 6 months paid parental leave A range of flexible working options Staff study assistance and paid study leave Ongoing professional development support Fitness Passport Corporate discount on health insurance Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling) Well-equipped modern facilities and contemporary workspaces with access to on-site childcare and medical services at our Townsville and Cairns’ campuses HOW TO APPLY Click the Apply button to be redirected to the JCU Careers Page and complete the following steps: Complete the online application form. Upload your current resume. Submit a cover letter outlining your relevant experience and how your skills and capabilities will contribute to your success in the role. Applications close Sunday 6th September 2026 at 11:55 PM AEST. ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process has been finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. James Cook University encourages people from all backgrounds who meet the role requirements to apply. We value and celebrate the diversity of our community and are committed to providing a safe, inclusive and welcoming learning and working environment. Back to job listing Recommended for you Grounds Officer Townsville Professional Enjoy working outdoors while helping maintain and enhance the vibrant tropical landscapes that make JCU unique. Head of Dentistry Cairns Academic Lead JCU's discipline of Dentistry and help shape the future of dental education, research and clinical practice across northern Australia and beyond. Research Worker Townsville Professional Provide essential operational and laboratory support to ensure project milestones are delivered efficiently and to a high standard. Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
    },
    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/head-of-dentistry-cairns-qld-australia": {
      "title": "We're Hiring!",
      "description": "Head of Dentistry - Cairns, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Head of Dentistry 495753 Cairns Academic Full time Closing on: Sep 27 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Full-time - 36.25 hours per week | Continuing Appointment Academic Level D/E 17% Superannuation plus excellent benefits incl. Clinical Loading, Leave Loading and Flexible Work Arrangements Lead the future of dentistry in Northern Australia James Cook University (JCU) is seeking an accomplished dental academic and clinician to lead our Discipline of Dentistry and help shape the future of dental education, research and clinical practice across northern Australia. As Head of Dentistry , you will have the opportunity to provide strategic and academic leadership for a dynamic discipline within JCU’s College of Medicine and Dentistry. You will work closely with the Dean, academic and professional colleagues, students, clinical partners and external stakeholders to strengthen the discipline’s teaching, research and clinical profile and ensure our programs continue to meet the needs of the communities we serve. This is an opportunity to make a genuine difference – through the education of the next generation of dental professionals, the development of innovative research and partnerships, and a strong commitment to improving health outcomes for rural, remote and underserved communities. Shape innovative and socially accountable dental education You will lead the delivery and continued development of high-quality largely undergraduate dentistry programs, fostering an innovative and supportive learning environment and ensuring the ongoing accreditation of our programs. Working across the College and University, you will: Provide strategic leadership and direction for the Discipline of Dentistry. Lead the delivery and continuous improvement of undergraduate and postgraduate dental education. Foster a high-quality clinical learning environment for students and staff. Strengthen the discipline’s research profile and create opportunities for collaboration, external funding and research partnerships. Build strong relationships with professional organisations, Hospital and Health Services, government, industry and the broader community. Contribute to the strategic direction and leadership of the College and University. Lead and support a diverse team, managing resources and creating an environment where staff and students can thrive. Make an impact where it matters JCU’s College of Medicine and Dentistry is committed to strengthening healthcare for the communities of northern Australia and beyond. Our programs are designed to produce health professionals who aspire to make a difference, with a particular focus on rural, remote and underserved communities, tropical health, and the health of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples. Based in Cairns , you will be part of a multidisciplinary academic environment where education, research, clinical practice and community engagement come together. The role provides an opportunity to build meaningful partnerships across northern Australia while contributing to the broader national and international profile of JCU Dentistry. Bring your expertise and leadership We are looking for an established dental academic and clinician who can combine academic leadership, clinical credibility and a strong commitment to education. You will bring: Higher qualifications in Dentistry and extensive clinical experience. Significant experience in tertiary dental education, including coordination and teaching of undergraduate and/or postgraduate programs. Strong leadership, organisational and business management capability, including experience leading staff. A substantial research record, including success in attracting external research funding and developing collaborative research initiatives. Highly developed communication and relationship-building skills, with the ability to represent and promote dentistry across the University and with professional, government, industry and community stakeholders. Current registration with the Dental Board of Australia as a dental practitioner. Experience with the Australian health system and dental service provision in rural and remote communities will be highly regarded, as will established relationships across the Australian dental education and professional sector. For appointment at Academic Level E, candidates will demonstrate national standing in academic dentistry education or specialist dentistry training and/or be recognised as a leading authority with outstanding academic leadership and achievement in dentistry or dental education. Keep one foot in clinical practice Importantly, this is a leadership role that remains connected to clinical practice. You will contribute at least three clinical teaching sessions each week in the JCU Dental clinic, providing an opportunity to continue sharing your clinical expertise directly with students and colleagues. Why JCU? At JCU, your leadership can have an impact well beyond the University. You will be joining an institution with a distinctive commitment to northern Australia and a strong focus on producing health professionals equipped to work with rural, remote and underserved communities. This is your opportunity to: Lead a discipline with an important role in the future of dental education and healthcare. Shape innovative, socially accountable dental education. Build research, industry, government and community partnerships. Develop the next generation of dental professionals. Make a difference to health and healthcare across northern Australia and beyond. Join us If you are an experienced dental academic and clinician ready to provide strategic leadership, champion excellence in education and research, and make a lasting contribution to dentistry in northern Australia, we would welcome your application. Apply now to lead the Discipline of Dentistry at James Cook University. How to Apply To discuss this opportunity and the application process in confidence, please contact Professor Sarah Larkins, Dean, College of Medicine and Dentistry on +61 7 4781 5025 or via email – deancmd@jcu.edu.au our body text Click the ‘Apply’ button or visit the JCU Careers Page and follow these steps: Complete the online application form Upload your current resume Upload a cover letter outlining your experience and how your skills align with the role Back to job listing Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 0:00 Loaded : 0% Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 0:00 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles captions and subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Apply Now First Name (required) 3bac2ef6 Last Name (required) a9947c03 Email (required) c54b1de1 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended for you Grounds Officer Townsville Professional Enjoy working outdoors while helping maintain and enhance the vibrant tropical landscapes that make JCU unique. Research Worker Townsville Professional Provide essential operational and laboratory support to ensure project milestones are delivered efficiently and to a high standard. Casual Collection Assistant Cairns Professional Looking for flexible work while you study? Join the Cairns Library team and make a positive impact on the student experience. Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
