    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/grounds-officer-townsville-qld-australia-eaccddd3-c453-4c04-b685-6db6f0ccbc35": {
      "title": "We're Hiring!",
      "description": "Grounds Officer - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Grounds Officer 495803 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Sep 20 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description James Cook University (JCU) is creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally. We now have an exciting opportunity for a dynamic and experienced Grounds Officer to join our Estate team. Full Time, continuing role | 36.25 hours per week. Based at our Townsville Bebegu Yumba campus HEWL 3: $63,640 - $71,188 per year plus up to 17% employer superannuation contributions, leave loading and other generous employee benefits ABOUT THE ROLE Join our dedicated team at James Cook University (JCU) and help create a safe, sustainable, and visually appealing campus environment. As a Grounds Officer based at our Townsville campus, you’ll play a vital role in maintaining and enhancing the University’s outdoor spaces, ensuring they showcase the beauty of our tropical setting and provide a welcoming environment for students, staff, and visitors. Maintain and improve campus grounds through landscaping, arboriculture and mowing. Operate and maintain irrigation systems, treat invasive flora, and support botanic development programs. Perform minor maintenance tasks on external signage, pathways, and hardscapes. Collaborate with the Estate team to plan annual maintenance activities and respond to emergencies. Promote sustainability initiatives through TropEco and uphold JCU’s values of respect, equity, and reconciliation. WHAT YOU CAN BRING TO THE ROLE You will bring proven experience in grounds maintenance or hold a Certificate II or higher in Horticulture or Landscape Construction (preferred). You have practical knowledge of gardening equipment, including ride-on mowers & chainsaws, irrigation systems, basic plant ID, and herbicide application. You can follow a scheduled maintenance plan in a large-scale environment and demonstrate strong teamwork and communication skills, with a commitment to safety and customer service. A current QLD C Class Driver’s Licence and the ability to meet the physical requirements of the role are essential. Find out more about JCU and our locations . WHY JCU? JCU offers a dynamic and culturally diverse workplace where your ideas are valued, your professional growth is supported, and your work-life balance is respected. Working under the values of Authenticity, Excellence, Integrity, and Respect , we support and empower our people through the provisions of; A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper 5 weeks of annual recreation leave plus leave loading 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year Up to 6 months paid parental leave A range of flexible working options Staff study assistance and paid study leave Ongoing professional development support Fitness Passport Corporate discount on health insurance Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling) Well-equipped modern facilities and contemporary workspaces with access to on-site childcare and medical services at our Townsville and Cairns’ campuses HOW TO APPLY Click the ‘apply’ button to be redirected to the JCU careers page and follow the below steps: Complete the application form Upload your current resume Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience. Applications close on Sunday, 20th September 2026 at 11:55 PM AEST . For any enquiries about the role, please contact Brandan Espe - brandan.espe@jcu.edu.au James Cook University encourages people from all backgrounds who meet role requirements to apply.  We value and celebrate the diversity of our community, and are committed to ensuring our community, and are committed to ensuring our learning and working environment is safe and welcoming. ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. Back to job listing Recommended for you Head of Dentistry Cairns Academic Lead JCU's discipline of Dentistry and help shape the future of dental education, research and clinical practice across northern Australia and beyond. Research Worker Townsville Professional Provide essential operational and laboratory support to ensure project milestones are delivered efficiently and to a high standard. Casual Collection Assistant Cairns Professional Looking for flexible work while you study? Join the Cairns Library team and make a positive impact on the student experience. Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
    },
    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/financial-services-officer-townsville-qld-australia-dcaacded-7134-4da8-91a2-43d3b7e84da0": {
      "title": "We're Hiring!",
      "description": "Financial Services Officer - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Financial Services Officer 495656 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Sep 6 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description James Cook University (JCU) is creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally Are you a detail-oriented financial professional with a passion for accuracy and customer service? Join our team as a Financial Services Officer and play a vital role in ensuring seamless financial processing and exceptional service delivery. Full-time, continuing position Based at the Townsville Bebegu Yumba campus, Douglas HEWL 4: $72,701 - $77,229 per annum plus up to 17% employer superannuation contributions, leave loading and other generous employee benefits. WHAT YOU CAN ACCOMPLISH IN THE ROLE Join a collaborative team dedicated to delivering exceptional financial services that support the success of JCU's students, staff, suppliers, and wider community. You'll play a key role in ensuring financial information is accurate, transactions are processed efficiently, and stakeholders receive timely, professional support that helps keep the University operating smoothly. With exposure to a broad range of financial activities, you'll build expertise in customer service, financial processing, data integrity, vendor and debtor management and compliance. You'll also have the opportunity to contribute ideas that enhance processes, improve customer experiences, and drive continuous improvement, making a meaningful impact on the delivery of financial services across the University. WHAT YOU CAN BRING TO THE ROLE We're looking for someone who enjoys working with numbers, takes pride in getting the details right, and is committed to delivering exceptional customer service. You will bring experience in financial transaction processing, a sound understanding of financial policies and procedures, and confidence using financial systems, ideally Finance One. Strong communication and interpersonal skills will help you build positive relationships with stakeholders and respond effectively to a variety of enquiries. Experience working in a higher education or corporate environment will be highly regarded. If you're someone who enjoys solving problems, working as part of a supportive team, and contributing to continuous improvement, we'd love to hear from you. Join us at JCU and help deliver quality financial services that support the success of our university community. SHAPE YOUR FUTURE WITH JCU At JCU we’re not just shaping minds; we’re shaping the future. As Australia’s only university established to focus on the issues of Northern Australia and the Tropics worldwide, JCU is dedicated to helping the world’s tropical regions to prosper. With our main campuses located in the vibrant and diverse tropics of Northern Queensland, JCU is at the forefront of research and education in some of the world’s most critical areas, including marine biology, environmental science, tropical and rural health, and more. Find out more about JCU , our Careers and our locations . WHY JCU? JCU offers a dynamic and culturally diverse workplace where your ideas are valued, your professional growth is supported, and your work-life balance is respected. Working under the values of Authenticity, Excellence, Integrity, and Respect , we support and empower our people through the provisions of; A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper 36.25-hour full-time working week 5 weeks of annual recreation leave plus leave loading 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year A range of flexible working options Attractive options for salary packaging Professional development support Fitness Passport Corporate discount on health insurance Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling) Well-equipped modern facilities and contemporary workspaces with access to on-site childcare, medical, gym and cafes HOW TO APPLY AND CONTACT DETAILS Are you ready to make a difference? Join us at JCU, where your future meets the tropics. Click the ‘apply’ button to be redirected to the JCU careers page and follow the below steps: Complete the application form Upload your current resume Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience in relation to the key requirements of the role and how your skills and experience will ensure your success. Applications close on Sunday 6th September 2026 at 11:55 PM AEST . For any enquiries about the role, please contact Curtis Moon at curtis.moon@jcu.edu.au ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. WHAT MATTERS TO US AT JCU Our People - Our staff, students, and the communities we serve Our Education - Knowledge has the power to change lives Our Place – the Tropics and beyond Our Research – a catalyst for innovation and knowledge generation James Cook University encourages people from all backgrounds who meet role requirements to apply.  We value and celebrate the diversity of our community, and are committed to ensuring our community, and are committed to ensuring our learning and working environment is safe and welcoming. Back to job listing Recommended for you Grounds Officer Townsville Professional Enjoy working outdoors while helping maintain and enhance the vibrant tropical landscapes that make JCU unique. Head of Dentistry Cairns Academic Lead JCU's discipline of Dentistry and help shape the future of dental education, research and clinical practice across northern Australia and beyond. Research Worker Townsville Professional Provide essential operational and laboratory support to ensure project milestones are delivered efficiently and to a high standard. Sign up for Job Alerts First Name (required) 879302c7 Last Name (required) 53fb3fc3 Email (required) 2b2f5891 Job Alert aabf301a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Treasury & Corporate Finance Treasury & Corporate Finance Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Townsville, QLD, Australia Townsville, QLD, Australia Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
