    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/research-worker-townsville-qld-australia-a7ca0870-2eea-4689-9ecc-a143622cf106": {
      "title": "We're Hiring!",
      "description": "Research Worker - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Research Worker 495665 Townsville Professional Part time Closing on: Sep 6 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Part time - 29 hours per week Fixed term contract to 10 September 2027 HEWL 4 $72,701 - $77,229 + 17% Super & great benefits Based in Townsville Join a collaborative research team contributing to nationally significant NHMRC‑funded work on improving diagnostics and genotyping for Strongyloides stercoralis . This role offers hands‑on laboratory experience and the opportunity to support impactful tropical health research. As a Research Worker, you’ll provide essential operational and laboratory support to ensure project milestones are delivered efficiently and to a high standard. You’ll work closely with senior researchers, assist with project coordination, and support PhD and Master’s students as needed. You’ll undertake a variety of laboratory tasks, including culture, microscopy, faecal concentration techniques, DNA extraction, PCR, electrophoresis, specimen reception and management. The role also includes placing purchase orders, managing inventory and reagent stocks, and supporting research administration and reporting. We’re looking for someone with strong organisational skills, attention to detail, confidence working in a laboratory environment, and the ability to collaborate effectively within a multidisciplinary research team. Why Join JCU? Join a university that’s deeply connected to its community and committed to improving health outcomes in rural, remote, and underserved regions. At JCU, you’ll be part of a vibrant academic environment that values diversity, equity, and sustainability.  We offer: 5 weeks annual leave + leave loading Flexible working arrangements Up to 6 months paid parental leave Salary packaging options Staff study assistance & paid study leave Fitness Passport & health insurance discounts Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching & counselling) Ongoing professional development support How to Apply and Contact Details If you’re keen to build your research skills, contribute to meaningful tropical health outcomes, and work in a supportive team, we’d love to hear from you. Click the ‘Apply’ button or visit the JCU Careers Page and follow these steps: Complete the application form Upload your current resume Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience and how your skills align with the role For further information, contact Associate Professor Richard Bradbury on 4781 4248  or via email richard.bradbury@jcu.edu.au Apply now and help advance vital research improving diagnostics for vulnerable communities. JCU celebrates diversity and is committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and welcoming environment for all. We encourage applications from people of all backgrounds who meet the role requirements. Back to job listing Recommended for you Grounds Officer Townsville Professional Enjoy working outdoors while helping maintain and enhance the vibrant tropical landscapes that make JCU unique. Head of Dentistry Cairns Academic Lead JCU's discipline of Dentistry and help shape the future of dental education, research and clinical practice across northern Australia and beyond. Casual Collection Assistant Cairns Professional Looking for flexible work while you study? Join the Cairns Library team and make a positive impact on the student experience. Sign up for Job Alerts First Name (required) efecac93 Last Name (required) a4eaeee5 Email (required) f167a6c2 Job Alert d829758a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments College of Medicine & Dentistry College of Medicine & Dentistry Employment Type Part time Part time Locations Townsville, QLD, Australia Townsville, QLD, Australia Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
    },
