    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/digital-spaces-engineer-cairns-qld-australia": {
      "title": "We're Hiring!",
      "description": "Digital Spaces Engineer - Cairns, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Digital Spaces Engineer 495565 Cairns Professional Full time Closing on: Sep 20 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally, and globally, James Cook University (JCU) now has an exciting opportunity for a Digital Spaces Engineer to join our team in the Technology Solutions directorate. Full-time, continuing opportunity | 36.25 hours per week. HEWL 6: $90,821 - $98,369 plus up to 17% employer superannuation contributions. Located in North Queensland - Cairns: Nguma-bada Campus, Smithfield. WHAT YOU CAN ACCOMPLISH IN THE ROLE We're looking for a Digital Spaces Engineer to help deliver exceptional technology experiences across James Cook University's learning, teaching and collaboration environments. If you're passionate about audio visual, videoconferencing and collaboration technologies and enjoy solving technical challenges, this is your opportunity to support innovative digital spaces that enable staff and students to thrive. You'll support the delivery, maintenance and continuous improvement of JCU's digital spaces portfolio, ensuring reliable and fit-for-purpose audio visual and videoconferencing experiences across the University. Support the performance of JCU's digital and physical spaces through the implementation, configuration and maintenance of audio-visual technologies. Provide technical expertise to diagnose and resolve complex AV and digital spaces issues, delivering high-quality customer service and support. Contribute to the successful delivery of AV projects through testing, commissioning and implementation activities. Drive continuous improvement by identifying recurring issues and supporting enhancements to services, processes and technologies. Assist in the design and enhancement of AV solutions by providing technical input and supporting the development of fit-for-purpose outcomes. WHAT YOU CAN BRING TO THE ROLE To succeed in this role, you'll need: A degree in Information Technology or a related discipline, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and training. Experience supporting, configuring and troubleshooting audio visual, videoconferencing or collaboration technologies in a complex environment. Knowledge of AV control systems, collaboration platforms and supporting infrastructure. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to investigate issues and prioritise competing demands. Well-developed communication and interpersonal skills, with a commitment to delivering exceptional customer service. Experience with technologies such as Cisco, Extron, Q-SYS, Biamp, Logitech, Microsoft Teams Rooms or Zoom Rooms will be highly regarded. WHY JCU? JCU offers a culturally diverse working environment with opportunities for professional and personal growth. Employee wellbeing is at the core of our values, and we support our people through the provision of flexible working conditions and many other exclusive benefits including; • A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper • 5 weeks of annual recreation leave • Annual leave loading • 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year • Up to 6 months paid maternity leave • 36.25-hour full-time working week • Flexible working options • Attractive options for salary packaging • Staff study assistance and paid study leave • Ongoing professional development support • Career enhancement opportunities • Fitness Passport • Corporate discount on health insurance • Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling) HOW TO APPLY Click the 'Apply' button to be redirected to the JCU Careers website and: Complete the application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant skills, experience and suitability for the role. Applications close Sunday, 20th September at 11:55pm AEST. ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. Back to job listing Recommended for you Grounds Officer Townsville Professional Enjoy working outdoors while helping maintain and enhance the vibrant tropical landscapes that make JCU unique. Head of Dentistry Cairns Academic Lead JCU's discipline of Dentistry and help shape the future of dental education, research and clinical practice across northern Australia and beyond. Research Worker Townsville Professional Provide essential operational and laboratory support to ensure project milestones are delivered efficiently and to a high standard. Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
    },
