    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/team-leader-hdr-program-support-townsville-qld-australia": {
      "title": "We're Hiring!",
      "description": "Team Leader, HDR Program Support - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Team Leader, HDR Program Support 495219 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Sep 13 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Full time - 36.25 hours per week | Continuing position HEWL 7 $99,878 - $110,446 + 17% super and great benefits Based in Townsville Help shape the future of research at JCU. We’re looking for a dynamic and motivated Team Leader to guide our HDR Program Support Team and deliver exceptional services to Higher Degree Research candidates and supervisors across the University. In this pivotal role, you’ll lead a small, high-performing team responsible for providing efficient, accurate and consistent academic and administrative support. You’ll coordinate workloads and priorities, streamline processes, and act as a key escalation point for complex queries—ensuring our HDR community receives outstanding service at every step. You’ll contribute to strategic planning within the Graduate Research School, drive continuous improvement initiatives, and support compliance, reporting and audit requirements through high-quality data analysis and documentation. Your ability to build strong relationships, influence stakeholders and lead with authenticity will be central to your success. What you’ll bring A relevant degree or equivalent experience in academic or research administration. Proven leadership capability, with experience developing teams and fostering a culture of service excellence. Strong organisational skills and the ability to manage competing priorities and complex projects. Excellent written communication and analytical skills, with confidence preparing reports and procedural documentation. Advanced interpersonal and negotiation skills, with the ability to work effectively across diverse areas of the University. Strong problem‑solving skills and sound judgement in resolving complex operational issues. Confidence using enterprise systems, databases and digital tools to support workflow efficiency. Join a university committed to excellence, sustainability, reconciliation and delivering a brighter future for the Tropics. If you’re passionate about leading people, improving processes and supporting research success, we’d love to hear from you. How to Apply and Contact Details Apply now and help empower the next generation of researchers at JCU. Click the ‘Apply’ button or visit the JCU Careers Page and follow these steps: Complete the application form Upload your current resume Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience and how your skills align with the role Applications close: 14 September 2025 For further information, contact Gabby Ryan via email gabby.ryan@jcu.edu.au JCU celebrates diversity and is committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and welcoming environment for all. We encourage applications from people of all backgrounds who meet the role requirements. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) e488338c Last Name (required) 5597f8ad Email (required) fc2516ab Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended for you Grounds Officer Townsville Professional Enjoy working outdoors while helping maintain and enhance the vibrant tropical landscapes that make JCU unique. Head of Dentistry Cairns Academic Lead JCU's discipline of Dentistry and help shape the future of dental education, research and clinical practice across northern Australia and beyond. Research Worker Townsville Professional Provide essential operational and laboratory support to ensure project milestones are delivered efficiently and to a high standard. Sign up for Job Alerts First Name (required) 293e81b4 Last Name (required) b701e00d Email (required) 37d50e68 Job Alert 445fe2eb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown 