    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/lecturer-senior-lecturer-social-work-cairns-qld-australia-townsville": {
      "title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Social Work",
      "description": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Social Work - Cairns, QLD, Australia - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Social Work 495676 Cairns Townsville Academic Full time Closing on: Sep 27 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Full time - 36.25 hours per week | Continuing Appointment Academic Level B - $112,810 - $133,110 Academic Level C - $137,166 - $157,465 17% Super, 5 weeks annual leave, leave loading & other great benefits Can be based in either Cairns or Townsville Are you passionate about shaping the future of Social Work in the Tropics? James Cook University is seeking an inspiring academic to join our Social Work team and contribute to high‑quality teaching, impactful research, and meaningful community engagement across Northern Queensland. As a Lecturer or Senior Lecturer, you’ll play a key role in developing and delivering innovative curriculum across our Social Work and Human Services programs, including the Bachelor of Social Work, Bachelor of Human Services, and Master of Social Work (Professional Qualifying). You’ll help create inclusive, student‑centred learning experiences that prepare graduates for contemporary practice in diverse communities. You will also contribute to JCU’s research strengths by producing high‑quality publications, pursuing external funding opportunities, and supervising Higher Degree Research candidates. Your work will support strong partnerships with community agencies, field education providers, and professional bodies, helping to enhance placement opportunities and strengthen JCU’s presence across the region. This is an opportunity to join a collegial, supportive team committed to excellence in teaching, research, and community impact—aligned with JCU’s Strategic Intent and our commitment to reconciliation, sustainability, and equity. What you’ll bring A PhD (or pathway to completion) in Social Work, Human Services or a related discipline. Successful experience teaching Social Work or cognate programs using contemporary, inclusive pedagogies across online, blended and face‑to‑face modes. A developing or established research profile with ERA‑recognised publications and a clear research agenda. Experience contributing to field education learning and supporting students on placement. Strong collaboration skills and the ability to work effectively within teaching, research and community engagement teams. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the capacity to represent JCU’s Social Work programs externally. Why Join JCU? Join a university that’s deeply connected to its community and committed to improving health outcomes in rural, remote, and underserved regions. At JCU, you’ll be part of a vibrant academic environment that values diversity, equity, and sustainability.  We offer: 5 weeks annual leave + leave loading Flexible working arrangements Up to 6 months paid parental leave Salary packaging options Staff study assistance & paid study leave Fitness Passport & health insurance discounts Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching & counselling) Ongoing professional development support How to Apply and Contact Details If you’re ready to make a meaningful contribution to Social Work education and research in a region where your work truly matters, we’d love to hear from you. Click the ‘Apply’ button or visit the JCU Careers Page and follow these steps: Complete the application form Upload your current resume Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience and how your skills align with the role For further information, contact Professor Lucy Jordan on 4232 1276  or via email lucy.jordan@jcu.edu.au Apply now and help shape the next generation of Social Workers in the Tropics. JCU celebrates diversity and is committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and welcoming environment for all. We encourage applications from people of all backgrounds who meet the role requirements. Back to job listing Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 2:09 Loaded : 0% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 2:09 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Apply Now First Name (required) d9af4eaf Last Name (required) f1c1546a Email (required) ec4f78e8 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended for you Grounds Officer Townsville Professional Enjoy working outdoors while helping maintain and enhance the vibrant tropical landscapes that make JCU unique. Head of Dentistry Cairns Academic Lead JCU's discipline of Dentistry and help shape the future of dental education, research and clinical practice across northern Australia and beyond. Research Worker Townsville Professional Provide essential operational and laboratory support to ensure project milestones are delivered efficiently and to a high standard. Sign up for Job Alerts First Name (required) e68b8790 Last Name (required) eaa23bdf Email (required) 8fb6ca82 Job Alert 68186026 Finalize your job 