    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/business-services-accountant-townsville-qld-australia": {
      "title": "We're Hiring!",
      "description": "Business Services Accountant - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Business Services Accountant 495740 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Sep 8 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description James Cook University (JCU) is creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally. Join James Cook University as a Business Services Accountant and help shape sound financial and governance outcomes across our controlled entities portfolio. Working closely with senior stakeholders, boards and business leaders, you'll deliver financial insights, support governance processes, and contribute to effective reporting and decision-making that strengthens organisational performance. Full-time continuing opportunity | 36.25 hours per week Based at the Townsville Bebegu Yumba campus Successful candidate must be based in Townsville or willing to relocate before commencement. HEWL 8: $111,960.56 - $128,567.19 per annum plus up to 17% superannuation ABOUT THE ROLE This role sits at the intersection of finance, governance and strategic support. As the Business Services Accountant, you'll oversee the financial reporting and governance activities of JCU's controlled entities, ensuring accurate financial information, robust compliance practices and effective board operations. From preparing financial and management reporting to coordinating governance cycles and company secretariat activities, you'll help provide the information, insights and support needed for confident decision-making across the portfolio. You'll also contribute to continuous improvement initiatives that enhance the consistency, efficiency and effectiveness of reporting and governance practices. WHAT YOU WILL BRING TO THE ROLE You are a financially astute and highly organised professional who can confidently navigate complex accounting, reporting and governance environments. You bring strong analytical capability, sound judgement and the ability to translate financial information into clear and meaningful insights for a range of stakeholders. Your collaborative approach, communication skills and ability to build productive relationships will enable you to work effectively with boards, business leaders and colleagues, while balancing competing priorities and maintaining a strong focus on accuracy, compliance and continuous improvement. WHY JCU JCU offers a dynamic and culturally diverse workplace where your ideas are valued, your professional growth is supported, and your work-life balance is respected. Working under the values of Authenticity , Excellence , Integrity , and Respect , we support and empower our people through the provisions of; A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper 5 weeks of annual recreation leave plus leave loading 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year Up to 6 months paid parental leave A range of flexible working options Staff study assistance and paid study leave Ongoing professional development support Fitness Passport Corporate discount on health insurance Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling) Well-equipped modern facilities and contemporary workspaces with access to on-site childcare and medical services at our Townsville and Cairns’ campuses HOW TO APPLY Are you ready to make a difference? Join us at JCU, where your future meets the tropics. Click the ‘apply’ button to be redirected to the JCU careers page , create an applicant account and follow the steps below: Complete the application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience in relation to the key requirements of the role and how your skills and experience will ensure your success in the role. For any enquiries about the role, please contact Tash Fraser at tash.fraser@jcu.edu.au Applications close Tuesday, 8th September 2026 at 11:55 PM AEST. ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. James Cook University encourages people from all backgrounds who meet the role requirements to apply. We value and celebrate the diversity of our community and are committed to providing a safe, inclusive and welcoming learning and working environment. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) a84d0fe8 Last Name (required) 23aba72f Email (required) 2a575f42 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended for you Grounds Officer Townsville Professional Enjoy working outdoors while helping maintain and enhance the vibrant tropical landscapes that make JCU unique. Head of Dentistry Cairns Academic Lead JCU's discipline of Dentistry and help shape the future of dental education, research and clinical practice across northern Australia and beyond. Research Worker Townsville Professional Provide essential operational and laboratory support to ensure project milestones are delivered efficiently and to a high standard. Sign up for Job Alerts First Name (required) 4cfacefc Last Name (required) eb0ab953 Email (required) 35cf7553 Job Alert b0eb9ce1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Treasury & Corporate Finance Treasury & Corporate Finance Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Townsville, QLD, Australia Townsville, QLD, Australia Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 19