    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/teaching-support-officer-cairns-qld-australia-11436f38-490a-401e-9ded-a1cb9f91adfa": {
      "title": "Teaching Support Officer",
      "description": "Teaching Support Officer - Cairns, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Teaching Support Officer 495744 Cairns Professional Full time Closing on: Sep 13 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Are you organised, detail-oriented, and passionate about supporting education? Join us as a Teaching Support Officer based on campus at JCU’s Cairns Nguma-bada campus and play a key role in ensuring the effective preparation and delivery of teaching activities. You will provide essential administrative, coordination, and data management services, contributing to the success of academic programs and Colleges. HEWL 5: $78,740 - $89,310 + up to 17% employer superannuation contributions. Two full time, continuing position | 36.25 hours a week On-campus, face-to-face position located at the Cairns Nguma-bada campus in North Queensland WHAT YOU CAN ACCOMPLISH IN THE ROLE As the Teaching Support Officer, you will play a key role in supporting the quality and consistency of teaching and learning practices. You will work with academic colleagues to facilitate the preparation of subject materials, maintain accurate subject information, and collaborate with teams across campuses to ensure alignment with internal processes and external regulatory requirements.  Your attention to detail and strong organisational skills will ensure efficient and effective outcomes in these areas. WHAT YOU WILL BRING TO THE ROLE Your strong communication skills, both written and verbal, will allow you to work effectively with a diverse range of stakeholders. You will demonstrate a high level of attention to detail, along with confidence in using Microsoft Office and other digital systems or databases essential to the role. You will have experience delivering high-quality customer service, especially in managing a high volume of enquiries. Your ability to resolve issues efficiently and provide clear, accurate advice will be key in supporting students and staff alike. HOW TO APPLY Are you ready to make a difference? Click the ‘apply’ button to be redirected to the JCU careers page and follow the below steps: Complete the application form Upload your current resume Upload a cover letter outlining your experience For further information regarding the role contact Sandra - (INT’L) +61 7 47815955 or via email on sandra.saunders@jcu.edu.au Applications close on Sunday, 13th September at 11.55pm. ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. WHAT MATTERS TO US AT JCU Our People - Our staff, students, and the communities we serve Our Education - Knowledge has the power to change lives Our Place – the Tropics and beyond Our Research – a catalyst for innovation and knowledge generation James Cook University encourages people from all backgrounds who meet role requirements to apply.  We value and celebrate the diversity of our community, and are committed to ensuring our community, and are committed to ensuring our learning and working environment is safe and welcoming. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) d72b2e07 Last Name (required) 1e74dabb Email (required) c9d0e4e7 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended for you Grounds Officer Townsville Professional Enjoy working outdoors while helping maintain and enhance the vibrant tropical landscapes that make JCU unique. Head of Dentistry Cairns Academic Lead JCU's discipline of Dentistry and help shape the future of dental education, research and clinical practice across northern Australia and beyond. Research Worker Townsville Professional Provide essential operational and laboratory support to ensure project milestones are delivered efficiently and to a high standard. Sign up for Job Alerts First Name (required) 3b3cdd64 Last Name (required) ce610a49 Email (required) 31d38209 Job Alert 4f64a8cf Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Education Design, Quality & Standards Education Design, Quality & Standards Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Cairns, QLD, Australia Cairns, QLD, Australia Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
