    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/hr-advisor-townsville-qld-australia": {
      "title": "We're Hiring!",
      "description": "HR Advisor - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! HR Advisor 495763 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Sep 6 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Make a difference through contemporary HR practice At James Cook University (JCU), our HR team is building something exciting, and we are seeking an enthusiastic, agile and customer-focused Human Resources Advisor to join our HR Partnerships team. This is a unique opportunity to be part of a team designed with people at its centre. You will help shape a modern, responsive and trusted HR service that supports leaders and staff across the University and delivers a seamless experience at every stage of the employee lifecycle. As a trusted member of the team, you will provide practical, accurate and contemporary advice across a diverse range of people matters, including employee relations, performance, organisational change, industrial interpretation, job design and workforce planning. You will also contribute to talent acquisition activities for allocated portfolios. Working in partnership with leaders and the broader HR team, you will provide advice and support across recruitment planning, attraction, selection and onboarding, helping JCU deliver compliant processes and an engaging customer and candidate experience. If you thrive on supporting others, embrace change with confidence and enjoy finding smart, practical solutions, we would love to hear from you. What you’ll do In this varied role, you will: provide timely and accurate advice to leaders and staff on contemporary HR practices, employment legislation, JCU’s Enterprise Agreement, policies and procedures coach and support leaders to effectively lead, manage and support their people across the employee lifecycle provide advice and case management support relating to employee relations, performance, workplace matters and organisational change assist leaders with workforce and recruitment planning, job analysis, job design and position evaluation support recruitment activities, including attraction strategies, selection processes, and pre-employment requirements and onboarding, whilst promoting a positive and inclusive candidate experience. use workforce and recruitment data, reporting and analytics to support informed decision-making build productive relationships across JCU and work collaboratively with HR colleagues and specialist teams develop and facilitate information sessions and training on contemporary HR practices and employee entitlements contribute ideas and practical solutions to continuously improve HR services, systems and processes. What you’ll bring You will have: relevant human resources qualifications and demonstrated experience providing generalist HR advice within a complex organisation in-depth knowledge of contemporary HR practices, employment legislation and industrial instruments experience advising on employee relations matters, HR case management, recruitment, job analysis, job design and evaluation experience supporting recruitment and selection processes and delivering positive customer and candidate outcomes the ability to interpret and clearly explain legislation, industrial instruments, policies and procedures strong relationship-building, communication, coaching and influencing skills excellent organisational and problem-solving skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities experience using HR or e-recruitment systems, reporting and data to support decisions and service improvement a collaborative, adaptable and customer-focused approach. Experience facilitating HR training or information sessions would be highly regarded. Why JCU? James Cook University is Australia’s only university dedicated to the tropics, with a clear purpose to create a brighter future for the people of Northern Australia and beyond. Our values—Authenticity, Excellence, Integrity, and Respect—are at the heart of everything we do, shaping how we work together and how we support our communities. What we offer a supportive, inclusive, and values-driven workplace where your contribution is recognised the opportunity to help shape and influence a contemporary HR partnerships model ongoing learning, development, and career growth opportunities a flexible, people-focused working environment that supports balance and wellbeing the chance to contribute to meaningful outcomes for staff, students, and the broader community If you’re ready to be part of a forward-thinking team and make a genuine impact, we encourage you to apply and bring your unique perspective to JCU. HOW TO APPLY AND CONTACT DETAILS Are you ready to make a difference? Join us at JCU, where your future meets the tropics. Click the ‘apply’ button to be redirected to the JCU careers page and follow the below steps: Complete the application form Upload your current resume Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience in relation to the key requirements of the role and how your skills and experience will ensure your success in the role. Applications close on Sunday 06 September, 2026. For any enquiries about the role, please contact Nicole Skipsey – Nicole.skipsey@jcu.edu.au If you are experiencing any issues with the Apply link from an external job board, please apply directly via our Careers Page . James Cook University encourages people from all backgrounds who meet role requirements to apply.  We value and celebrate the diversity of our community, and are committed to ensuring our community, and are committed to ensuring our learning and working environment is safe and welcoming. ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) c8c5caef Last Name (required) 951c2c03 Email (required) 732a4e04 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended for you Grounds Officer Townsville Professional Enjoy working outdoors while helping maintain and enhance the vibrant tropical landscapes that make JCU unique. Head of Dentistry Cairns Academic Lead JCU's discipline of Dentistry and help shape the future of dental education, research and clinical practice across northern Australia and beyond. Research Worker Townsville Professional Provide essential operational and laboratory support to ensure project milestones are delivered efficiently and to a high standard. Sign up for Job Alerts First Name (required) fe5b2ea1 Last Name (required) 74e90c9a Email (required) baf93569 Job Alert 0eb7acc9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Human Resources Human Resources Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Townsville, QLD, Australia Townsville, QLD, Australia Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
