    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/expression-of-interest-veterinary-clinical-academic-opportunities-townsville-qld-australia": {
      "title": "We're Hiring!",
      "description": "Expression of Interest – Veterinary Clinical Academic Opportunities - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Expression of Interest – Veterinary Clinical Academic Opportunities 492687 Townsville Academic Full time Closing on: Sep 6 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Shape the Future of Veterinary Science in the Tropics World-Class Veterinary Science. Tropical Lifestyle. Endless Opportunity. Join us as we shape one of Australia's most exciting Veterinary Science programs. Join one of the world's most distinctive veterinary schools and help tackle the animal, agricultural and biosecurity challenges that matter most to Northern Australia and the tropics. At James Cook University (JCU), our Veterinary Science program is recognised for its strong industry partnerships, hands-on clinical training, tropical focus and commitment to animal, human and environmental health. JCU is also actively contributing to animal health, zoonotic disease surveillance, biosecurity research and the development of the next generation of veterinary professionals. We're embarking on an exciting period of growth and are seeking talented academics, clinicians and leaders to join our world-class Veterinary Science team. This is more than a career opportunity—it's a chance to influence the future of veterinary education, drive impactful research, and prepare graduates to meet the evolving needs of animals, communities and industries across northern Australia and beyond. As we continue to grow our program, we're seeking Expressions of Interest from passionate academics and clinicians who want to be part of something exceptional. Opportunities include: Equine Medicine Companion Animal Internal Medicine Veterinary Anaesthesia Small Animal Surgery Veterinary Anatomy / Veterinary Career Development (VCD) Veterinary Public Health Animal Welfare and Behaviour Deputy Head of Discipline Why JCU Veterinary Science? Make a genuine impact Educate future veterinarians while contributing to research and clinical practice that improves animal health, biosecurity and community outcomes across Australia and the tropics. Work where others holiday Enjoy an enviable tropical lifestyle in North Queensland, with access to the Great Barrier Reef, ancient rainforests and vibrant regional communities. Collaborate across disciplines Work alongside experts in veterinary science, biosecurity, animal health, One Health, public health and environmental sciences to address complex global challenges. Advance your career Whether you're an emerging academic, an experienced clinician or an established leader, JCU offers opportunities to build your teaching, research, leadership and clinical profile. Be part of a supportive culture Join a collegial team that values innovation, collaboration, academic excellence and real-world impact. Who We're Looking For We are seeking passionate professionals who are committed to: Delivering outstanding veterinary education Contributing to impactful research and scholarship Building industry and community partnerships Supporting student success and graduate employability Advancing animal health, welfare and sustainable veterinary practice For leadership opportunities, including Deputy Head of Discipline – Veterinary Science , we are looking for individuals who can inspire teams, drive academic excellence and help shape the future direction of veterinary education and research at JCU. Why JCU? As Australia's university for the Tropics, JCU is uniquely positioned to tackle the veterinary challenges of the future—from biosecurity and emerging diseases to livestock production, wildlife health and companion animal care. Working at JCU means you'll enjoy: The opportunity to help shape a growing Veterinary Science program from the ground up. A collaborative culture that values innovation, leadership and impact. Support to grow your teaching, research and clinical profile. Modern facilities and strong industry partnerships. Competitive salary packages with 17% employer superannuation, generous leave, and excellent salary ranges — with additional loadings available for select roles — to reward the right talent. An enviable tropical lifestyle in North Queensland, with world-class natural environments on your doorstep. Make Your Mark at JCU Whether your expertise is in specialist clinical disciplines, veterinary public health, animal welfare, diagnostics or academic leadership, this is your opportunity to join a university making a difference where it matters most. Express your interest today and help shape the future of veterinary science in Northern Australia and beyond. How to Express your Interest Please apply directly via the via the JCU careers page and follow the below steps: Complete the application form Upload your current resume For any enquiries about these positions, please contact Associate Professor John Cavalieri, Head of Veterinary Science on +61 7 4781 4438 or via email john.cavalieri@jcu.edu.au . Or please contact Louise Zupp, Talent Acquisition Advisor on +61 7 4232 1120 or via email louise.zupp@jcu.edu.au Back to job listing Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 3:07 Loaded : 0% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 3:07 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Tra