    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/casual-eoi-laboratory-and-technical-support-townsville-qld-australia-cairns": {
      "title": "We're Hiring!",
      "description": "Casual EOI - Laboratory and Technical Support - Townsville, QLD, Australia - Cairns, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Casual EOI - Laboratory and Technical Support 495002 Cairns Townsville Professional Casual Closing on: Oct 31 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Expression of Interest – Casual Laboratory and Technical Support Creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally, James Cook University (JCU) is seeking Expressions of Interest for Laboratory and Technical Support to support practical learning and  teaching activities across a variety of discipline areas including medicine, nursing and allied health, engineering, animal handling, aquaculture and across the sciences. What You Can Accomplish in the Role In this role, you will deliver high-quality technical support that enables undergraduate and postgraduate teaching to achieve academic objectives, helping to provide students with a hands-on, practical learning experience. You will contribute to: Supporting undergraduate classes, field trips, intensives, and workshops, ensuring activities are delivered on time and in accordance with established procedures. Maintaining safe and compliant teaching and research environments through cleaning, waste management, equipment servicing, and sterilisation. Ensuring Workplace Health and Safety (WHS) requirements are understood and adhered to within laboratory settings. Providing guidance to staff and students on laboratory procedures, policies, and relevant legislative requirements. Supporting continuous improvement by contributing to service enhancements and evaluating user outcomes and satisfaction. What You Can Bring to the Role You are a proactive and reliable professional with strong technical and organisational skills, and a commitment to delivering high-quality support services. You will bring: Relevant qualifications and/or experience related to the discipline Experience in standard laboratory and/or field techniques, including familiarity with common laboratory and field equipment. Sound understanding of WHS legislation and its practical application within laboratory environments. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities and deadlines. Effective communication and interpersonal skills, with a commitment to delivering a customer-focused service. Ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a high-volume environment. Strong computer skills, including Microsoft Office, and the ability to learn new systems quickly with attention to detail. Additional Requirements Current First Aid Certificate Current Queensland C Class Driver Licence Current Working with Children Blue Card Specific certifications and vaccinations may be required for some roles* Why Submit an Expression of Interest? This Expression of Interest will be used to establish a talent pool for upcoming opportunities within JCU. If you’re passionate about supporting teaching and research through technical expertise, we encourage you to apply. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 838a4be0 Last Name (required) 02de1277 Email (required) 5d78a604 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended for you Grounds Officer Townsville Professional Enjoy working outdoors while helping maintain and enhance the vibrant tropical landscapes that make JCU unique. Head of Dentistry Cairns Academic Lead JCU's discipline of Dentistry and help shape the future of dental education, research and clinical practice across northern Australia and beyond. Research Worker Townsville Professional Provide essential operational and laboratory support to ensure project milestones are delivered efficiently and to a high standard. Sign up for Job Alerts First Name (required) 81d366c3 Last Name (required) 25f25fe4 Email (required) 8cb75d92 Job Alert 2cd4b4ab Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Academic Services Academic Services Employment Type Casual Casual Locations Cairns, QLD, Australia Townsville, QLD, Australia Cairns, QLD, Australia Townsville, QLD, Australia Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
